<div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">The acquisition method, with a genuinely distinctive cost-relief alternative</div><div class="principle">ASPE Section 1582 governs the RECOGNITION and MEASUREMENT of BUSINESS combinations – REQUIRING the ACQUISITION method for TRANSACTIONS in WHICH an ACQUIRER obtains CONTROL of ONE or MORE businesses. THE core MECHANICS closely MIRROR IFRS 3 internationally, BUT the SUBSEQUENT treatment of GOODWILL includes a GENUINELY distinctive PRIVATE-enterprise alternative NOT available under UNMODIFIED IFRS (Section 7).</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope – Transactions Where an Acquirer Obtains Control</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Applies wherever control transfers from one party to another</div><div class="principle">This Section applies TO transactions or EVENTS in WHICH an ACQUIRER obtains CONTROL of ONE or MORE businesses – REGARDLESS of WHETHER the RESULTING subsidiary is SUBSEQUENTLY consolidated OR accounted for USING the COST or EQUITY method under SECTION 1591.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>The Acquisition Method</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Fair value measurement of the acquiree's identifiable net assets</div><div class="text-supporting">THE acquisition METHOD requires IDENTIFYING the ACQUIRER, DETERMINING the ACQUISITION date, and RECOGNIZING the IDENTIFIABLE assets ACQUIRED, liabilities ASSUMED, and ANY non-CONTROLLING interest AT fair VALUE as OF the ACQUISITION date.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>Identifying the Acquirer and the Acquisition Date</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">The party obtaining control, and the date control transfers</div><div class="text-supporting">THE ACQUIRER is the ENTITY that OBTAINS control OF the ACQUIREE – GENERALLY identifiable AS the party TRANSFERRING cash or OTHER assets, OR incurring LIABILITIES, in EXCHANGE for CONTROL. THE ACQUISITION date is the DATE the ACQUIRER OBTAINS control OF the ACQUIREE, TYPICALLY the CLOSING date OF the transaction.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>Measuring Identifiable Assets, Liabilities, and Non-Controlling Interest</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Fair value as of the acquisition date</div><div class="text-supporting">IDENTIFIABLE assets ACQUIRED and LIABILITIES assumed ARE recognized SEPARATELY from GOODWILL, MEASURED at THEIR acquisition-DATE fair VALUES. ANY non-CONTROLLING interest IN the ACQUIREE is ALSO measured AT fair VALUE as OF the ACQUISITION date.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>Measuring and Recognizing Goodwill</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Consideration transferred plus NCI, less net identifiable assets</div><div class="text-supporting">GOODWILL is MEASURED as the EXCESS of (a) the CONSIDERATION transferred PLUS the AMOUNT of ANY non-CONTROLLING interest, OVER (b) the FAIR value OF the ACQUIREE'S identifiable NET assets ACQUIRED – CONSISTENT with IFRS 3'S own GOODWILL calculation INTERNATIONALLY.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>THE DISTINCTIVE ALTERNATIVE – the Private-Enterprise Goodwill Amortization Election</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">A cost-relief alternative unavailable under unmodified IFRS</div><div class="text-supporting">RECOGNIZED goodwill IS SUBSEQUENTLY measured UNDER Section 3064 – WHERE, GENUINELY distinctively, an ENTERPRISE MAY elect to AMORTIZE goodwill ON a straight-LINE basis OVER its ESTIMATED useful LIFE (NOT exceeding TEN years WHERE a LIFE cannot BE reliably ESTIMATED), TESTING for IMPAIRMENT only UPON indicators OF impairment, RATHER than MANDATORY ANNUAL impairment TESTING. THIS stands IN genuine CONTRAST to the IMPAIRMENT-only model IFRS 3/IAS 36 REQUIRE, and INTERESTINGLY parallels a SIMILAR "private COMPANY alternative" the FASB'S Private COMPANY Council INTRODUCED for US GAAP – BOTH standard-SETTERS independently CONCLUDING that ANNUAL, mandatory GOODWILL impairment TESTING imposes a GENUINELY disproportionate COST burden on PRIVATE enterprises RELATIVE to its DECISION-usefulness for THEIR typically NARROWER user BASE.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Negative Goodwill (Bargain Purchase Gain)</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Recognized immediately, after reassessment</div><div class="text-supporting">WHERE the FAIR value OF the ACQUIREE'S net IDENTIFIABLE assets EXCEEDS the CONSIDERATION transferred (a "BARGAIN purchase"), the ACQUIRER first RE-ASSESSES whether IT has CORRECTLY identified ALL assets ACQUIRED and LIABILITIES assumed, and CORRECTLY measured THEIR fair VALUES – WITH any REMAINING excess RECOGNIZED immediately AS a GAIN in NET income.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Acquisition-Related Costs – Expensed as Incurred</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Not capitalized into the cost of the combination</div><div class="text-supporting">COSTS the ACQUIRER incurs IN connection WITH a BUSINESS combination (LEGAL fees, DUE diligence COSTS, advisory FEES) are EXPENSED as INCURRED – EXCEPT costs OF issuing DEBT (per SECTION 3856) or EQUITY securities (per SECTION 3610), WHICH are ACCOUNTED for UNDER their OWN respective SECTIONS.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Worked Example – Recognizing Goodwill at Acquisition</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">The standard goodwill calculation</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: An arm's-length acquisition</div><div class="wk-body">A private company acquires 100% of an unrelated target for $8,500,000 cash. The target's identifiable net assets have a fair value of $6,900,000.</div><div class="wk-answer">GOODWILL = $8,500,000 − $6,900,000 = <strong>$1,600,000</strong>, recognized ON the BALANCE Sheet, SUBJECT to Section 3064'S subsequent MEASUREMENT policy (IMPAIRMENT-only, OR the AMORTIZATION alternative, PER the COMPANY'S accounting POLICY election).</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Worked Example – Amortizing Goodwill Under the Private-Enterprise Alternative</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">A predictable, straight-line expense over an estimated useful life</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: Electing straight-line amortization</div><div class="wk-body">Continuing the prior example, the company elects to amortize its $1,600,000 goodwill on a straight-line basis over an estimated 10-year useful life.</div><div class="wk-answer">The company RECOGNIZES annual GOODWILL amortization EXPENSE of $1,600,000 ÷ 10 = <strong>$160,000 per year</strong>, TESTING for IMPAIRMENT only UPON indicators OF impairment ARISING – RATHER than PERFORMING a MANDATORY annual IMPAIRMENT test.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">What Section 1582 requires</div><div class="check-list"><span>Name and description of the acquiree, acquisition date, and consideration transferred</span><span>Amounts recognized for identifiable assets acquired, liabilities assumed, and goodwill (or bargain purchase gain)</span><span>Goodwill's subsequent measurement policy – impairment-only, or the amortization alternative and its estimated useful life</span></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2"><div class="ctitle cn">Where judgment matters most</div>
<div class="two-col"><div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGMENTS</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Identifying the acquirer in a combination</span><span>Whether to elect the goodwill amortization alternative, and the resulting estimated useful life</span></div></div>
<div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Fair value of identifiable assets acquired and liabilities assumed</span><span>Fair value of any non-controlling interest</span></div></div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Relationship to IFRS 3</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Comparison – ASPE Section 1582 vs IFRS 3</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Feature</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-warning);">ASPE Section 1582</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-info);">IFRS 3</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Acquisition method core mechanics</span><span>Same framework</span><span>Same framework – converged</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Goodwill subsequent measurement</span><span>Impairment-only, OR amortization alternative</span><span>Impairment-only ONLY – no amortization option</span></div>
</div>
<div class="note">THE acquisition METHOD itself is GENUINELY thoroughly CONVERGED – the GOODWILL amortization ALTERNATIVE is the SINGLE most SIGNIFICANT, distinctly PRIVATE-enterprise-oriented divergence FROM unmodified IFRS.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s15"><span class="num">15</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Where every business combination event lands</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Goodwill recognition</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span></span><span>Subject to impairment testing, or amortization if elected</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Bargain purchase gain</span><span><span class="badge is">IS</span></span><span>Recognized immediately</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s16"><span class="num">16</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Section</span><span>Connection</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Section 1591</span><span>Subsidiaries – governs whether and how the resulting subsidiary is subsequently accounted for (consolidation, cost, or equity method)</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Section 3064</span><span>Goodwill and Intangible Assets – supplies the full subsequent measurement policy, including the amortization alternative</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s17"><span class="num">17</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2">
<div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Acquisition method</div><div class="glossary-def">The accounting method for a business combination, requiring fair value measurement of identifiable assets acquired, liabilities assumed, and any non-controlling interest.</div></div>
<div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;"><div class="glossary-term">Goodwill amortization alternative</div><div class="glossary-def">An accounting policy election permitting a private enterprise to amortize goodwill on a straight-line basis over its useful life, rather than testing it for impairment annually.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="legend"><div class="ltitle">Financial statement key (ASPE terminology)</div><div class="lrow"><div class="litem"><span class="badge bs">BS</span> Balance Sheet </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge is">IS</span> Income Statement </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge sre">SRE</span> Statement of Retained Earnings / Statement of Changes in Equity </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge scf">SCF</span> Cash Flow Statement</div></div></div>


</div>
